### Quick Install
```bash
composer require maslosoft/mangan
```





<!--/header-->

Mangan maps PHP objects to MongoDB documents using active documents or plain PHP
models. This branch requires **PHP 8.5 or newer**, the MongoDB PHP extension 2.x,
and the runtime extensions declared in `composer.json`.

Read [Getting started](docs/getting-started/index.md) for a complete model and
connection example, [Configuration](docs/configuration/index.md) for named
connections, and [Application servers](docs/application-servers/index.md) for
Light contexts and worker cleanup. Upgrade existing applications using the
[PHP 8.5 migration guide](docs/upgrading/php-85/index.md), including the EmbeDi 3
dependency and required companion source fix. That
EmbeDi fix has not been published yet; the current migration must be developed
with the fixed local dependency checkout.

For library work, see [Development and testing](docs/development/index.md).
The maintained [mangan skill](.agents/skills/mangan/SKILL.md) covers application usage;
[mangan-dev](.agents/skills/mangan-dev/SKILL.md) covers development of this library.

